  "_acceptedAdvisories": [
    "GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (brace-expansion, unbounded expansion causing OOM) is",
    "knowingly accepted. It covers everything up to 5.0.7 and was never",
    "backported, so no 1.x or 2.x release is clean. Forcing 5.0.8 through",
    "overrides does not work: minimatch 3 and 4 do `require('brace-expansion')`",
    "and call the result, while 5.0.8's CommonJS build exports a named `expand`,",
    "which breaks ESLint with 'expand is not a function'. The affected copies",
    "reach us only through minimatch and glob inside build tooling, which sees",
    "nothing but glob patterns written in this repository, so there is no",
    "untrusted input path. Revisit when those packages ship a compatible",
    "brace-expansion."
  ]
